{% doc %}
  Renders the `--block-padding-{top,bottom,left,right}` CSS custom
  properties from a block's padding settings. Must be called from inside a
  `{% style %}...{% endstyle %}` tag.

  Reads Horizon's logical padding keys first (`padding-block-start`,
  `padding-block-end`, `padding-inline-start`, `padding-inline-end` — looked
  up via bracket notation because the hyphens in their names are not valid
  Liquid dot-notation identifiers), falling through to this theme's own
  physical keys (`padding_top`, `padding_bottom`, `padding_sides`) when a
  block's schema has no logical key. Horizon has no separate left/right
  field — its single `padding_sides` covers both, which is why both inline
  fallbacks read the same old key. A block only has the keys its own schema
  declares; unset/undeclared keys resolve to `nil` in Liquid and fall
  through via the `default` filter. An explicit `0` is not blank in Liquid's
  `default` filter (it only replaces `nil`, `false`, and empty
  strings/arrays), so a logical key explicitly saved as `0` wins and does
  not fall through to the physical key.

  @param {object} block - required. The section or block whose `settings` supplies the logical or physical padding keys.
  @param {number} [top_default] - Default px for the top/block-start padding when unset. Defaults to 0.
  @param {number} [bottom_default] - Default px for the bottom/block-end padding when unset. Defaults to 0.
  @param {number} [sides_default] - Default px for the left/right/inline padding when unset. Defaults to 0.

  @example
  {%- style -%}
    #shopify-block-{{ block.id }}.shopify-block {
      {%- render 'block-padding-vars', block: block -%}
    }
  {%- endstyle -%}
{% enddoc %}
--block-padding-top: {{ block.settings["padding-block-start"] | default: block.settings.padding_top | default: top_default | default: 0 }}px;
--block-padding-bottom: {{ block.settings["padding-block-end"] | default: block.settings.padding_bottom | default: bottom_default | default: 0 }}px;
--block-padding-left: {{ block.settings["padding-inline-start"] | default: block.settings.padding_sides | default: sides_default | default: 0 }}px;
--block-padding-right: {{ block.settings["padding-inline-end"] | default: block.settings.padding_sides | default: sides_default | default: 0 }}px;
